lisa-design:
- Step 1 extraction rationale: package internal/api/handler/oscal imports internal/api/handler, so lineage.go (package handler) cannot import oscal. The leverage projection/aggregation was extracted to a NEUTRAL internal/service/leverage package (imports relational, relational/risks, converters/labelfilter only; never internal/api). oscal keeps thin behavior-preserving wrappers/aliases so every existing endpoint/test is byte-for-byte unchanged: upstreamResponsibility = leverage.Responsibility (alias), leveragedControlProjection = leverage.Projection (alias), bulkResolveUpstreamResponsibilities/deriveSatisfaction/projectLeveragedControls/computeDedupeKeyForLeverageDrift are wrappers, ResponsibilityPosture is an exported wrapper. Do NOT re-inline these into oscal — the whole point is the neutral home.
- Evidence status logic moved to relational/evidence.go: EvidenceStatusCountsForFilters (was oscal.getStatusCountsForFilters body) + CollapseEvidenceStatus (was computeProfileControlStatus body). oscal.getStatusCountsForFilters now maps relational.StatusCount -> ProfileComplianceStatusCount; computeProfileControlStatus delegates. leverage.ResponsibilityPosture uses the relational funcs directly. This keeps one definition shared by oscal + leverage without an import cycle.
- Credit rule is split by design. leverage.AggregateByControl.Credit encodes ONLY ">=1 link AND all links active AND all links live-derived full". The other two pinned conditions — "evidence collapse is unknown" and "control in scope" — are applied by the CONSUMERS, deliberately not in the aggregate: derivePosture consults inheritedCredit only after the evidence switch and after the !inScope early-return; the compliance-progress handler only flips unknown->inherited; complianceFor's single-SSP fallback gates on e.inScope(ref). Evidence always wins in both directions as a result.
- derivePosture is now 4-arg (added inheritedCredit bool). PostureInherited slots BETWEEN the evidence switch and the impl-status switch — ladder: out-of-scope > not-satisfied(ev) > satisfied(ev) > inherited > not-applicable > planned > attention. Credit is checked on ref ITSELF only (assessSSP), never rolled up through the implements-closure; parents pick inherited leaves up through postureCountsFor/sspBreakdownForSet leaf tallies (matches how satisfied/not-satisfied roll up). assessCache memo stays sound because the aggregates are deterministic per engine build.
- leverage.Summarize live-derives satisfaction via DeriveSatisfaction from the current satisfied rows, NEVER the stored ssp_leverage_links.satisfaction column (which can rot when the upstream changes its responsibility set). It is deliberately lighter than Project (no per-responsibility posture, no drift risk id) so it can run on every lineage engine build (~7 bulk queries, guarded by lineage_perf_integration_test).
- Leverage matching is by control-id ONLY (UPPER-folded, no catalog id), via leverage.NormalizeControlID — same established precedent as implStatusBySSP / implemented requirements. ControlKey{SSPID, ControlID}. Accepted trade-off: same-id controls across catalogs can cross-match (same exposure as implStatusBySSP).
- ProfileComplianceControlLeverage.Inherited (and the lineage LineageLeverageSummary presence) reflect credit-worthiness / link-existence independent of the displayed status. The leverage badge is emitted whenever >=1 link exists (credit or not) so partial/drifted/revoked leverage still surfaces; inherited:true means the links earned credit even if evidence overrode the computedStatus/posture.
- GET /api/lineage/nodes/:key/leverage uses guard.Read() (same as /ssps) — it exposes upstream SSP/offering titles + responsibility text to any lineage reader; accepted, consistent with /ssps. It builds a global engine buildEngine(nil,nil) only for downstream SSP titles + the 404 control-exists check; upstream SSP titles come from a separate Preload("Metadata") mirroring collectInheritedSharedResponsibility. Link JSON is byte-identical to oscal leveragedControlResponse + upstreamSspTitle inside inheritedFrom.
- inherited int fields are emitted non-omitempty (0 when no sspId) — intentional, backward compatible per the pinned contract.
